    "narrative": "For May 29th, the Austin Waves offense centers around the premier matchup for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22), who projects as our strongest play. Facing Triston Rogers, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor and a solid lineup spot in the three-hole, making him an anchor for Roto output today. Alongside him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) capitalize on elite matchups against Giolito and Melton, respectively. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically draws a +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile, while **Sam Antonacci**\u2014our primary weapon for the scarce stolen base category\u2014benefits from a prime leadoff spot and a strong xwOBA, keeping him in the elite tier despite a neutral park environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board involved the decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (46.33) in favor of the higher-efficiency projections found in our starting lineup. While **Coby Mayo** draws a significant park boost and has favorable platoon splits against Macko, his lower spot in the batting order ultimately pushed his score below the threshold required to displace starters like **Dominic Smith** (59.11) or **Nasim Nunez** (59.76). **Nasim Nunez** earns the nod today primarily for his utility as a speed-focused play; despite a lower order position, the matchup against Giolito offers enough volatility to justify the start in a 5x5 format where steals remain the primary bottleneck for our team ceiling.\n\nManagers should remain wary of the heavy hitters forced into difficult matchups today, specifically **Gunnar Henderson** (52.11), **Andy Pages** (48.56), and **Kyle Tucker** (55.23). All three are facing Zack Wheeler or Macko, both of whom carry sub-3.00 xERA profiles that suppress the base projections for our stars. While **Kyle Tucker** and **Gunnar Henderson** are effectively \"must-starts\" due to their season-long floor, the risk of a sub-optimal day is elevated. **Liam Hicks** (49.09) also sits in a marginal zone, though his dynamic platoon advantage against Freddy Peralta provides just enough upside to maintain his spot behind the plate. Keep an eye on weather reports, as the wind conditions favoring the hitters provide a marginal hedge against the elite pitching we are facing tonight.",
